    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both accounts agree on the events; the case turns on how long the driver actually held position at the Tampines interchange PHV bay, measured the way the policy measures it.\n\nUnder POL-NS-01 a no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions hold, and the driver side must carry every one. Limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least the free waiting period in force - 300 seconds, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec - measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the driver's 07:38:05 arrival tap. The driver's own trace (EV-GPS-00209, weight 1.0) shows a single qualifying held run of 236 seconds, 07:44:14 to 07:48:10, ending exactly at the 07:48:10 cancellation: 64 seconds short of 300. Limb (c) fails and the fee is not chargeable.\n\nThe driver's 'more than ten minutes' is the trip record's wait_time_min of 10.1, but that figure runs from the 07:38:05 button marker, which POL-NS-01(c) does not accept as the start of the clock; the derived dwell_start_offset (-369 seconds) puts the start of the counted dwell at 07:44:14. The request to weigh the platform's 10.1 minutes against the trace's 236 seconds is therefore declined: the policy names one measurement and the trace supplies it, and the driver does not ask for the geometry to be recomputed. No traffic advisory covers the bay (EV-ADVIS-00209-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-NS-06(i) cannot sum separate in-geofence intervals and 236 seconds is the whole dwell.\n\nPOL-NS-06 therefore applies: the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded to the rider in full, with no driver compensation. The $6.00 fee has in fact already been refunded (EV-FARE-00209: refund_issued_sgd 6.00, payment_status REFUNDED). This dispute was filed by the driver to restore that fee. Under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION means the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands; on a driver-filed dispute over a fee the platform has already reversed, that leaves the rider refunded. That is the correct outcome: the driver's claim to the $6.00 is not supported and the refund stands. No money moves, so the ruling sits below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold.\n\nOn the remaining points. The driver's limbs (a), (b) and (d) arguments are partly right and do not help: limb (d) is satisfied (cancelled_by DRIVER, reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, no boarding event, no in-app calls) and the POL-NS-02 proximity test is met (25 qualifying fixes, closest approach about 30 m), but satisfying those limbs does not save the fee once limb (c) fails. The driver's point that no false-arrival referral arises is accepted: POL-NS-05(ii) needs no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere and there are 25, and the corrected dwell falls short of the minimum so no referral is produced in any event. The rider's POL-NS-04 point decides nothing - she sent no chat message, so limb (a) is not met and POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her, but she does not need it, because the fee fails on the dwell - and her track (88 fixes, all within 91.7 m of the pin) is consistent with her statement that she was at the bay. Driver compensation is refused: POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 displaces it here, so the SGD 4.80 the money block computes is not due. The anti-farming check itself does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 3, below the four-or-more limb; 3 of 88 completed trips is 3.4%, below the 8% limb) and the profile counters were read correctly - the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is context only and was not used - but this is beside the point once the fee does not stand. The argument that the correct instrument is DRIVER_COMPENSATION rather than NO_ACTION is rejected for the same reason: with the fee not chargeable there is no payout to name, and NO_ACTION on a driver-filed dispute over an already-reversed fee is exactly the disposition POL-GEN-03 describes.\n\nWeight and confidence. The deciding fact - the 236-second dwell - is carried by EV-GPS-00209 at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02 cap is 1.0 and confidence is 0.95. EV-CHAT-00209 is impaired at weight 0.85 (issue UNREAD_MESSAGE; both driver messages and the system notice carry read_at null), and that impairment is disclosed, but the chat log does not carry the deciding fact and does not move the outcome or the cap. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence in a way no clause resolves, no repeat-party pattern appears, the anti-farming check does not trip, and the deciding artifact is not impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d). No clause produces a referral on these facts.",
