    "explanation": "To both parties: the record does not support restoring the $6.00 cancellation fee, so the refund already issued to the rider stands and the driver is paid nothing.\n\nWHAT THE RECORD SHOWS. This was a TRANSPORT_HUB pickup (Tampines Bus Interchange PHV bay), where the free waiting period in force is 300 seconds (EV-TRIP-00209, platform_policy.free_wait_sec 300), and the $6.00 fee is the correct zone figure (EV-FARE-00209, cancellation_fee 6.00, total_charged 6.00). The driver tapped 'arrived' at 07:38:05 and terminated at 07:48:10 recording RIDER_NO_SHOW (EV-TRIP-00209). The unbroken 10-second GPS trace (EV-GPS-00209, weight 1.0, 100% coverage, 108 fixes, no gaps) shows the driver's only qualifying in-geofence run inside the 150 m arrival radius running from 07:44:14 to 07:48:10: 236 seconds, 25 fixes, 64 seconds short of the 300-second minimum. POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix and not from the 'arrived' tap, and POL-NS-06 makes a dwell shorter than the free waiting period non-chargeable, with the fee refunded in full and no driver compensation. The driver's central argument, that trip_record.wait_time_min of 10.1 minutes should stand as the wait, is rejected: that figure is measured from the 07:38:05 button-press marker, which sits 369 seconds before the first qualifying in-geofence fix (EV-GPS-00209, dwell_start_offset_sec -369), and the policy does not accept it as the start of the dwell clock. POL-NS-12, which would let a platform-recorded arrival and wait timer carry that fact in its own right, applies only to GPS_AUTO arrivals; this record's marker is BUTTON, so it does not apply.\n\nPOINTS THAT SURVIVE BUT DO NOT CHANGE THE OUTCOME. Arrival is established on the trace (25 consecutive qualifying fixes; closest approach 30.3 m) and limb (d)'s substantive elements are present (cancelled_by DRIVER, code RIDER_NO_SHOW, no boarding, no in-app calls), so the claim that no one can say the driver never reached the bay is accepted. The rider's own POL-NS-04 route does not assist her either, because she sent no message and made no call, so limb (a) fails; her presence within 91.7 m of the pin is accepted but is not the deciding fact. None of this alters the result, because POL-NS-07 compensates the driver only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-06 displaces it here. The driver's request for $4.80 (80 per cent of the $6.00 fee) is therefore refused; the anti-farming check on driver_profile (no_show_terminations_30d 3 of completed_trips_30d 88, 3.4 per cent, and only those two counters are read) does not trip, so no escalation packet arises, and no compensation is payable because the fee itself is not chargeable.\n\nRULING. The dispute was filed by the driver over a fee the platform has already reversed (EV-FARE-00209: refund_issued_sgd 6.00, payment_status REFUNDED). POL-GEN-03 defines NO_ACTION party-relatively: on a driver-filed dispute over a fee already reversed it leaves the rider refunded and never restores the charge. That is the correct disposition here: the $6.00 refund stands and driver compensation is null. The monetary effect is $0.00, below the $8.00 execution threshold under POL-GEN-05.\n\nEVIDENCE INTEGRITY. EV-CHAT-00209 is impaired at weight 0.85, issue UNREAD_MESSAGE (both driver messages and the system arrival notice carry read_at null); it does not carry the deciding fact, so it does not cap confidence, and it corroborates the rider's account that she saw nothing until afterwards. EV-ADVIS-00209-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT: no traffic advisory covers this bay, so POL-NS-06(i) interval-summing is unavailable and the single 236-second run is the admissible dwell. The deciding fact, a 236-second dwell against a 300-second minimum, is carried by two independent weight-1.0 artifacts, the GPS trace and the trip record, so the confidence cap is 1.00; confidence is set at 0.90.\n\nREFERRALS. No clause produces one. POL-NS-05(ii)'s false-arrival record requires that no qualifying in-geofence fix exist anywhere on the trip, and 25 do; POL-NS-05's falsity trigger (more than 300 m from the pin, or 15 km/h or more at the marker timestamp) is not established by any derived fact at 07:38:05, so no false-arrival referral is made; and no reason code was mis-selected, RIDER_NO_SHOW being one of the three POL-NS-01(d) recognises. Both parties remain entitled to appeal under POL-GEN-04."
